  "family": "Myrtaceae",
  "memo": "This tree has a distinctive round canopy that provides ample shade. Its leaves are oval-shaped and have a striking blue-green color, adding a unique touch to urban landscapes. The bark peels in strips, revealing a smooth, cream-colored surface underneath, which gives the trunk a mottled appearance. During the blooming season, clusters of small, white flowers emerge, attracting bees and other pollinators. This tree is drought-tolerant and thrives in sunny locations, making it a practical choice for city streets and parks. Its aromatic leaves release a refreshing scent when crushed, adding to its appeal.",
