  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has round, bluish-green leaves that can be used to teach about leaf shapes and coloration. The leaves release a distinctive aroma when crushed, providing a sensory experience for students. Its bark peels off in strips, revealing a smooth, multicolored trunk underneath, which can be a talking point for discussions on bark texture and tree growth. The small, white flowers attract pollinators, offering an opportunity to explore plant-insect interactions.",
